          "date": "2026-11-13 12:30:18.000000000",
          "tz": 600
        },
        "subject": "DRAFT LU-21180 lod: add kunit test for defined striping",
        "message": "DRAFT LU-21180 lod: add kunit test for defined striping\n\nlod_use_defined_striping() builds the in-core layout (and the\nper-stripe dt_object array) from an already fully-defined on-disk LOV\nEA, as happens on replay of a layout-extend intent. It was untested.\n\nAdd lod_defined_striping_test.c, covering a plain LOV_MAGIC_V1 EA\n(every stripe instantiated in order), a LOV_MAGIC_V3 EA with a pool\nname (pool copied onto the component), and an EA with an unrecognized\nmagic (rejected with -EINVAL, no striping left behind). As in\nlod_init_obj_test, stripe instantiation is redirected to a canned\nmock_ost_obj per OST via a KUnit static stub on\nlod_lookup_stripe_object(), so no real OSD/OSP is needed.\n\nExport lod_use_defined_striping() and lod_striping_free(), needed by\nthe new test module, and register it in lustre/kunit/Makefile,\nKUNIT.modules_list and lod/KUNIT.list.\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial\nSigned-off-by: Ronnie Sahlberg <rsahlberg@whamcloud.com>\nAssisted-by: AGENT:claude-sonnet-5 [claude-code]\nChange-Id: I85b512e23e6ea391c0150e6927f4e823c89d823f\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
